==> [2/2] replication_demo.sh — streaming replica on port 5433, fully automated

=== 0. Clean slate (safe to re-run) ===

=== 1. Replication role + pg_hba lines at the TOP of pg_hba.conf ===
# P5 replication (added by replication_demo.sh)
local   replication   repl                              trust
host    replication   repl      127.0.0.1/32            trust
local   all           repl                              trust
# PostgreSQL Client Authentication Configuration File

=== 2. Base backup of the primary into the replica data directory ===
base backup complete: 117M

=== 3. Give the replica its own config (Ubuntu keeps config in /etc, so the backup has none) ===
standby.signal present: yes
primary_conninfo:      primary_conninfo = 'user=repl password=replpass channel_binding=prefer host=''/var/run/pos...

=== 4. Start the replica on port 5433 ===

=== 5. Who is who? (each query is run on a different server) ===
--- PRIMARY (port 5432) ---
